From 9b9894069a9d11b6ce865203eee301aadad61386 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 15:26:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] DOS-PORT: patch 0076 -- DOSAGS_FORCE_COLOR_DEPTH benchmarking
 override

WHY: PLAN.md's 32-bit display path KPI work (2026-09-15) needs same-
content fps numbers across color depths for two real 32-bit games
(Shards of God, IOAWN4T) to compare against a 40fps push target. Neither
game has an 8/16-bit-authored variant, and building a full "convert
32-bit assets to 16-bit at load" feature (Option 2 from PLAN.md's
"32-bit display path -- design comparison" section, explicitly NOT the
chosen production path when Option 1 was picked) turned out to need far
less new code than that section estimated once actually traced through
this pinned engine version.

WHAT: a single DOS-guarded (__DJGPP__) hook in engine_load_game_data(),
reading DOSAGS_FORCE_COLOR_DEPTH (8/16/32, in bits) and overwriting
game.color_depth (bytes-per-pixel: 1/2/4) immediately after
load_game_file() succeeds, before Bitmap::SetColorDepth() or any sprite/
room background is first touched. This one field flip is sufficient
because sprites already convert to game.GetColorDepth() generically on
every load (PrepareSpriteForUseImpl, Engine/ac/draw.cpp) via the sprite
cache, and -- a real correction to PLAN.md's own design-comparison
session, which only checked Common/game/roomstruct.cpp's FixBitmap()/
UpscaleRoomBackground() (width/height only, no depth) and concluded room
backgrounds needed a NEW conversion-at-load hook -- room backgrounds
ALREADY get the exact same treatment: load_new_room() (Engine/ac/
room.cpp) calls that same PrepareSpriteForUse() on every
thisroom.BgImages[i] right after the room file loads, a one-time
load-time cost already, not a per-frame one. No new conversion code was
needed for either sprites or backgrounds -- confirmed by reading both
call sites directly, not assumed from the earlier design session's own
conclusion (docs/patch-conventions.md's "a patch series' own stated
rationale is not evidence" applies here to a design DOC's rationale, not
just a patch series, but the same discipline).

VALIDATED on DOSBox-X against a real game (Shards of God, this session's
own local test copy): DOSAGS_FORCE_COLOR_DEPTH=16 renders the real title
screen correctly end to end (screenshot). DOSAGS_FORCE_COLOR_DEPTH=8
does NOT render correctly -- a real, separate, expected limitation, not
a bug in this patch: RoomBgFrame::Palette (Common/game/roomdata.h) is
"only valid in 8-bit games", so a 32-bit-authored room has no real
256-color palette for the existing depth-conversion code to quantize
against, and the result is a flat, wrong-color background. Operator
decision, same session: use Trilby's Notes (a real natively-8-bit game,
already a golden reference in this repo) for the 8-bit KPI datapoint
instead of building a color quantizer -- a materially bigger feature,
out of scope here.

NOT a shipped rendering path: this is a benchmarking/diagnostic-only
override, gated behind an env var nothing sets by default. The real
native 32-bit present path is ali3dsw.cpp's own support (patch 0075).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Kwnh5s6CDW7FKaod1cMR9Q
---
 Engine/main/engine.cpp | 56 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 56 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Engine/main/engine.cpp b/Engine/main/engine.cpp
index 041af5b36..f08bf7076 100644
--- a/Engine/main/engine.cpp
+++ b/Engine/main/engine.cpp
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 
 #include <errno.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
 #include <stdexcept>
 #if AGS_PLATFORM_OS_WINDOWS
 #include <process.h>  // _spawnl
@@ -453,6 +454,58 @@ void engine_init_exit_handler()
     atexit(atexit_handler);
 }
 
+#ifdef __DJGPP__
+// DOS-PORT (patch 0076): DOSAGS_FORCE_COLOR_DEPTH forces game.color_depth
+// to a value other than what the game was authored at, immediately after
+// load and before Bitmap::SetColorDepth() (below) -- i.e. before any
+// sprite or room background is first touched. Exists for same-content
+// fps comparison across depths (PLAN.md's 32-bit display path KPI work,
+// 2026-09-15); it is NOT a shipped rendering path -- the real native
+// 32-bit path is ali3dsw.cpp's own support (patch 0075). Values are in
+// BITS (8/16/32), matching how the rest of this port already talks about
+// depth (DisplayMode::ColorDepth), not game.color_depth's own
+// bytes-per-pixel storage unit -- converted here so the env var's
+// contract doesn't leak that internal representation detail.
+//
+// Why this one field flip is enough, with no further engine changes:
+// sprites already convert to game.GetColorDepth() generically on every
+// load (PrepareSpriteForUseImpl, Engine/ac/draw.cpp) via the sprite
+// cache, and room backgrounds do too -- confirmed by reading
+// load_new_room() (Engine/ac/room.cpp) directly, which calls that exact
+// same PrepareSpriteForUse() on every thisroom.BgImages[i] right after
+// the room file loads, a one-time load-time cost, not a per-frame one.
+// This corrects a real gap in PLAN.md's own design-comparison session
+// (2026-09-15): it read Common/game/roomstruct.cpp's FixBitmap()/
+// UpscaleRoomBackground() (which indeed only fixes width/height, never
+// depth) and concluded backgrounds had no load-time conversion step,
+// without also checking room.cpp's own separate background-preparation
+// call, which already does exactly this generically for any game --
+// the room-background gap that session flagged as still needed does not
+// actually exist in this pinned engine version.
+//
+// No RUNMANIFEST field added for this -- the existing DOSAGS_SCENE tag
+// already covers "what was this run" (e.g. DOSAGS_SCENE=depth32); adding
+// a second, narrower mechanism for the same purpose would be redundant.
+static void dos_apply_color_depth_override()
+{
+    const char *env = getenv("DOSAGS_FORCE_COLOR_DEPTH");
+    if (!env || !env[0])
+        return;
+    const int bits = atoi(env);
+    if (bits != 8 && bits != 16 && bits != 32)
+    {
+        Debug::Printf(kDbgMsg_Warn,
+            "DOS-PORT: DOSAGS_FORCE_COLOR_DEPTH=%s ignored (must be 8, 16, or 32)", env);
+        return;
+    }
+    const int native_bits = game.GetColorDepth();
+    Debug::Printf(kDbgMsg_Info,
+        "DOS-PORT: DOSAGS_FORCE_COLOR_DEPTH forcing game color depth %d -> %d bit (benchmarking override, not a shipped path)",
+        native_bits, bits);
+    game.color_depth = bits / 8;
+}
+#endif
+
 int engine_load_game_data()
 {
     Debug::Printf("Load game data");
@@ -464,6 +517,9 @@ int engine_load_game_data()
         display_game_file_error(err);
         return EXIT_ERROR;
     }
+#ifdef __DJGPP__
+    dos_apply_color_depth_override();
+#endif
     // Assign the default bitmap color depth, equals this game's color depth
     Bitmap::SetColorDepth(game.GetColorDepth());
     return 0;
-- 
